Read this with the RPC record count from spikes/results/pi-rpc-boundary-cost.log:
the session corpus is the *coarser* population (one record per message, not one
per streamed delta), so µs/record here is a floor on the RPC stream's count and a
ceiling on its per-record size. Any pass whose boundary cost is claimed to matter
has to beat the denominator in that log, not this one.
